# Also here, not only in .gitignore: pub reads .pubignore *instead of*
# .gitignore in the directory that has one, so nothing above is inherited.
# Measured before this line existed: the binary went into the dry-run file
# list and took the archive from 1 MB to 4 MB.
example/frame_cost
example/frame_cost.exe

# The demo animation is 1.79 MiB and was the whole of this package's download.
# It does not need to ship: pub.dev never reads README images out of the
# archive, it rewrites them to proxy the repository, so the file is fetched
# from GitHub raw whether or not it is in here. Keeping it out took the archive
# from 1.85 MiB to well under a tenth of that.
#
# Re-encoding it was measured and rejected instead of guessed. Animated WebP at
# q60 is 6% of the size, and it erases most of the connecting lines, which are
# the subject. Lossless animated WebP keeps them and still costs 1.49 MiB.
doc/demo.gif

# Sources for the two generated figures, and the blog diagram. The figures
# themselves are `screenshots:` entries and have to stay in the archive; their
# SVG is only needed to regenerate them, which tool/ does from scratch anyway.
doc/*.svg
doc/blog/
